{
  "description": "One tag per Archil error code, named after the code in PascalCase (`sandbox_fork_mounted` -> `SandboxForkMounted`). Each matches the status plus the body's `code`, and carries the body's text as `message`. Codes come from the spec's response examples, plus codes the live API returned that the spec omits (`sandbox_not_ready`, `sandbox_stop_conflict`, `sandbox_not_deletable`, `sandbox_has_forks`, `conflict` on createBranch, and `not_found` on every 404). Categories drive retries: `sandbox_pausing`, `sandbox_stopping` and `sandbox_not_ready` are retryable, `no_capacity` is retryable as throttling, and `not_enabled` declares no httpError so its 503 is not retried as a server error. The API token operations type their 401 as Unauthorized. Archil answers a bad key and a valid key it refuses with the same bare 401 `Unauthorized` (live, 2026-11-11: `GET /api/tokens` and `DELETE /api/tokens/{id}` refuse the key that lists disks with 200), so the tag names the status, not a cause.",
  "patches": [
